      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "ALPINE THUNDER (1) led and faded fresh over 1200m in similar grade, finishing sixth. Fitter and back to the sharper trip. Has the claim and will take catching. BILLIE THE GREAT (5) was a fresh-up winner then has placed in the three runs since. Long overdue and gets her chance to break through. EASTCOAST MISS (4) ran on well to place fresh then finished alongside ALPINE THUNDER last time. Key chance who should prove hard to beat. GEEGEES MISSILE (2) resumed in the same race and faded to finish well back. That was off a long break and has a decent second-up record. Has upside and yet to miss the frame this course and distance. NO ACCESS (8) has a light weight and will be winding up late.",
